-- DragonUI_NewEra/modules/collections/Data.lua — mount & companion SOURCE-INFO tables.
--
-- The 3.3.5a Companions API (GetCompanionInfo) returns only creatureID/name/spellID/icon — it has
-- NO description, source ("Vendor: … Zone: … Cost: …") or lore text. Retail's Mount/Pet Journal
-- shows those from a client-side DB. These two tables are that DB: PORTED VERBATIM from the
-- EZCollections addon's Data/Mounts.enUS.lua + Data/Pets.enUS.lua (the community-maintained
-- source strings), re-homed onto the DragonUI_NewEra namespace so this addon carries its own copy
-- and does NOT depend on EZCollections being installed/enabled at runtime.
--
-- ROW FORMAT (both tables), keyed by SPELL ID (the creatureSpellID GetCompanionInfo returns):
--   [1] creatureDisplayID   (unused — EZCollections' own Journal feeds this straight into
--                           ModelFrame:SetCreature for not-yet-learned rows, but SetCreature on
--                           THIS client only accepts a server-resolvable creature/unit reference,
--                           not a raw CreatureDisplayInfo.dbc id; tried and reverted)
--   [2] type/petTypeIcon    (unused)
--   [3] flags               (unused)
--   [4] name                (may be nil → fall back to the live API name)
--   [5] description / lore  (may be nil/"")
--   [6] sourceType          (unused)
--   [7] sourceText          (the coloured "Vendor: … Zone: … Cost: …" block; may be nil)
--
-- Consumers use NE.collections.GetInfo(kind, spellID) → name, lore, source.

local NE = DragonUI_NewEra
NE.collections = NE.collections or {}


